FYI: Many projects use issue templates to point you in the right direction. Reading the guidelines or issue templates before opening issues can save you and project maintainers valuable time. | SushiWaUmai (2024-01-28T21:14:02Z): I'm getting the same error, all I do is
```ts
import GhostContentAPI from "@tryghost/content-api";
import { BACKEND_URL, BACKEND_API_KEY } from "./constants";

const api = GhostContentAPI({
  url: BACKEND_URL,
  key: BACKEND_API_KEY,
  version: "v5.0",
});

export async function getPost(slug: string) {
  return await api.posts.read({ slug }).catch((err) => {
    console.error(err);
  });
}
```

And importing the above function like this: 
```tsx
export default async function Page({ params }: PageProps) {
  const post = await getPost(params.slug);
  ...
}
``` | 20manas (2024-02-27T17:07:23Z): I was able to fix it with this:
```typescript
const api = new GhostContentAPI({
  url: ...,
  key: ...,
  version: ...,
  makeRequest: async ({url, method, params, headers}) => {
    const apiUrl = new URL(url);
    Object.keys(params).map(key => apiUrl.searchParams.set(key, params[key]));

    return fetch(apiUrl.toString(), {method, headers})
      .then(async res => {
        if (!res.ok) {
          throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${res.status}, response data: ${await res.text()}`);
        }

        return {data: await res.json()};
      })
      .catch(error => {
        console.error('Fetch error:', error);
      });
  },
});
``` | tanayvaswani (2024-02-27T17:33:09Z): @20manas is it working with prod build? with strict set to true
 | 20manas (2024-02-28T10:36:55Z): @tanayvaswani yes, it's working just fine for me. Make sure to install `@types/tryghost__content-api` and it should work.

daniellockyer (2023-09-01T12:25:53Z): Hey there, thank you so much for the detailed bug report.

That does look like something that shouldn't happen! A PR to fix this issue would be very welcome 🙂 | iprasandeep (2023-09-07T23:15:16Z): Hi  @daniellockyer , @cathysarisky 

The issue with Google reporting that the page is not mobile responsive due to excessive width can be resolved by modifying the CSS  - 

```
.kg-layout-split .kg-header-card-text {
    padding: 12vmax 4vmax;
    max-width: 100%; 
    box-sizing: border-box;
}
```


max-width: 100%; -  This addition ensures that the header cards won't extend beyond the width of the viewport, addressing the issue where Google reports excessive width.

box-sizing: border-box; - This property ensures that padding is included within the defined width of the element, preventing padding from adding to the overall width.

Please let me know if could I fix this issue. I need guidance to set up Ghost locally on my machine. | cathysarisky (2023-09-08T03:28:59Z): Hey @iprasandeep , I believe this issue (which was bigger than just that one spot I saw it in) has been addressed recently in this commit:
https://github.com/TryGhost/Ghost/commit/c759f419a1868676b8e57fcffc36b4d1cb3b8732

If you need help settings up Ghost locally, please post over on forum.ghost.org.

